# .gcloudignore — what `gcloud run deploy --source backend` may NOT upload.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (2026-08-24): without it, gcloud INFERS an ignore set from
# backend/.gitignore. That inference probably did the right thing, but it is not a
# guarantee we control — and this directory contains a GCP SERVICE-ACCOUNT PRIVATE
# KEY and a .env holding OpenAI/Anthropic/xAI/LangSmith keys, DATABASE_URL and
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN. Uploaded source lands in the project's _cloudbuild staging
# bucket and PERSISTS there as a build artifact. "Probably excluded" is not the
# standard for a private key (CLAUDE.md §10 names these two filenames explicitly).
#
# The runtime image is unaffected by anything here: the Dockerfile copies ONLY
# `app/` and `requirements.txt`. Verified before writing this file — app/ contains
# ZERO .json files, and its two .md files are docs/debug output that no code reads
# (rendered_output.md is write-only, parser_render.py:676).

# ---- secrets: the reason this file exists ----
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
gen-lang-client-*.json
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json

# ---- virtualenvs & caches (also: keeps the upload small) ----
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---- the eval suites: fixtures, benchmarks, results, traces. Large, and never
# ---- part of the served app (the Dockerfile does not copy tests/).
tests/
scripts/

# ---- docs (owner-requested 2026-08-24): none are read at runtime ----
*.md

# ---- local run artifacts ----
logs/
temp/
*.log
.git/
.gitignore
